# Public API documentation

TypeDoc reads JSDoc on exported symbols (`packages/*/src/`, generated to `packages/*/docs/`).
Types come from TypeScript signatures — comments explain **meaning**, not types.

## Every public export

- One-line **summary** (required): what it does, not how.
- Prefer `{@link Symbol}` for cross-references (`createLegacyTx`, `StateManagerInterface`).
- v10 factories: document module-level `createX` functions; deprecated class constructors point to them via `@deprecated` + `@see`.

## `@param` / `@returns`

| Tag | Use when |
|-----|----------|
| `@param name` | Semantics, units, encoding, defaults, or EIP/hardfork conditions — **not** obvious from name + type |
| `@returns` | Return semantics not obvious from the type (`undefined` meaning, side effects, async init) |
| `@throws` | Invalid input throws (especially tx, util signing, fee/value fields) |
| `@example` | High-traffic entry points (`createVM`, `createLegacyTx`, `runBlock`) |

**Do not** use `@param {Type}` or `@returns {Type}` — legacy JS; TypeScript owns types.

**Skip** bare `@param opts` when `*Opts` / `*Data` interfaces document each property.

## Interfaces and options objects

Document non-obvious properties on the interface (`TxOptions`, `VMOpts`, `MPTOpts`), including defaults and when a field applies.

## Phase out

- `{Type}` in `@param` / `@returns`
- Name-only tags with no description (`@param blockData` alone)
- “Static factory methods” — say `createBlock`, `createLegacyTx`, etc.
- `{@link StateManager}` — use `{@link StateManagerInterface}` or a concrete impl

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ redundant types + bare param names
/**
 * @param {TxData} txData
 * @param {TxOptions} opts
 * @returns {LegacyTx}
 */

// ✅ summary + semantics; types from signature
/**
 * Instantiate a legacy transaction from a plain data object.
 *
 * All `txData` fields are optional; unsigned txs omit `v`/`r`/`s`.
 * Pass `opts.common` when the chain ID must match EIP-155 `v`.
 *
 * @throws If fee or value fields overflow or are non-numeric
 */

// ✅ options documented on the interface, not repeated on every factory
/** A {@link Common} instance; copied internally so HF changes do not leak. */
common?: Common
```

## Finish

After doc edits in touched packages: `npm run tsc` (per package or `--workspaces`) and spellcheck on changed files.
